<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><!-- version 2026-1: January 22, 2026 - Revised the overall XSD structure and added documentation references for additional information. There are no substantive XML format changes, other than the removal of the unused lineNumber attribute from the Context element. --><xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">	<xs:annotation>		<xs:documentation>This XSD defines the structure of the messages.xml file returned by the E-Filing system for batch submissions made via SFTP. After a batch is submitted, E-Filing validates the contents and reports whether the batch was accepted with no errors, accepted with errors, or rejected. For web-based batch filings, this information is available shortly after submission through Track Status. For SFTP submissions, the same validation results are provided in the messages.xml file, which is placed in the acks folder within the user’s home directory shortly after submission.The messages.xml file is NOT the formal acknowledgment (ACK) file. The ACK file is generated only after a submission is accepted and is typically made available within 1–2 business days. The messages.xml file allows batch filers to determine whether a submission was accepted or rejected and to identify any errors requiring action. This messages.xml is not mandatory to process, but is still returned for all submissions via SFTP.</xs:documentation>	</xs:annotation>	<xs:element name="BatchMessages">		<xs:complexType>			<xs:sequence>				<xs:element ref="Batch"/>			</xs:sequence>		</xs:complexType>	</xs:element>	<xs:element name="Batch">		<xs:complexType>			<xs:sequence>				<xs:element ref="Message" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>			</xs:sequence>			<xs:attribute name="type" type="sdtmBatchFormType" use="required"/>			<xs:attribute name="trackingID" type="xs:string" use="required">				<xs:annotation>					<xs:documentation>This value will be the tracking ID assigned by FinCEN to the batch submission. Examples: CXST26-00123456, REST26-00123456, etc.</xs:documentation>				</xs:annotation>						</xs:attribute>			<xs:attribute name="status" type="statusType" use="required"/>			<xs:attribute name="filingName" type="xs:string" use="required">				<xs:annotation>					<xs:documentation>This value will match the batch XML file name of the corresponding batch submission.</xs:documentation>				</xs:annotation>						</xs:attribute>			<xs:attribute name="filingDate" type="xs:date" use="required">				<xs:annotation>					<xs:documentation>This value will correspond with the date on which the batch was submitted to FinCEN in the format: YYYY-MM-DD where YYYY indicates the year, MM indicates the month, and DD indicates the day</xs:documentation>				</xs:annotation>						</xs:attribute>		</xs:complexType>	</xs:element>	<xs:element name="Message">		<xs:complexType>			<xs:sequence>				<xs:element name="Context" type="xs:string">				<xs:annotation>					<xs:documentation>This value identifies the element location (within the associated batch submission) that triggered the error. The value identifies the name and sequence number (in brackets) of the associated element’s parent element from the batch submission. The value can be up to 4000 characters. Example: EFilingBatchXML/Activity[1]/Party[25]/PartyIdentification[49]/PartyIdentificationNumberText</xs:documentation>				</xs:annotation>								</xs:element>				<xs:element ref="Description">				<xs:annotation>					<xs:documentation>This value is a brief description (usually 1-3 sentences, up to 512 characters) associated with the error. Refer to the error code list in the corresponding form type's batch technical guide for additional informaion.</xs:documentation>				</xs:annotation>				</xs:element>			</xs:sequence>			<xs:attribute name="level" type="severityLevelType" use="required"/>			<xs:attribute name="code" type="xs:string" use="required">				<xs:annotation>					<xs:documentation>This will be a multi-character code (usually 2-4 characters) associated with the error. Refer to the error code list in the corresponding form type's batch technical guide for additional informaion.</xs:documentation>				</xs:annotation>			</xs:attribute>		</xs:complexType>	</xs:element>	<xs:element name="Description" type="xs:string"/>	<xs:simpleType name="statusType">		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">			<xs:enumeration value="ACCEPTED">				<xs:annotation>					<xs:documentation>A batch file that receives a ACCEPTED status means that the batch, including all reports within the batch, are accepted by FinCEN with no errors generated. Accepted batches will receive a corresponding acknowledgement file, which will include the BSA ID assigned to each report within the batch, within 1-2 business days after submission acceptance.</xs:documentation>				</xs:annotation>			</xs:enumeration>			<xs:enumeration value="ACCEPTED-WITH-WARNINGS">				<xs:annotation>					<xs:documentation>A batch file that receives a ACCEPTED-WITH-WARNINGS status means that the batch, including all reports within the batch, are accepted by FinCEN; however, one or more reports in the batch have a received a WARNING error that should be reviewed. Refer to the error CONTEXT to determine the location of the error, and also refer to the error code list in the corresponding form type's batch technical guide to determine what action to take in response to the specific error code. Accepted with warnings batches will receive a corresponding acknowledgement file, which will include the BSA ID assigned to each report within the batch, within 1-2 business days after submission acceptance.</xs:documentation>				</xs:annotation>			</xs:enumeration>			<xs:enumeration value="REJECTED">				<xs:annotation>					<xs:documentation>A batch file that receives a REJECTED status means that the batch, including all reports within the batch, are NOT accepted by FinCEN. Refer to the error CONTEXT and DESCRIPTION to determine what action to take. Once the fatala error(s) are addressed in the batch, resubmit. Rejected batches will NOT receive a corresponding acknowledgement file.</xs:documentation>				</xs:annotation>			</xs:enumeration>		</xs:restriction>	</xs:simpleType>	<xs:simpleType name="severityLevelType">		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">			<xs:enumeration value="INFO">				<xs:annotation>					<xs:documentation>This error severity level is INFORMATION and does not require further action.</xs:documentation>				</xs:annotation>			</xs:enumeration>			<xs:enumeration value="WARN">				<xs:annotation>					<xs:documentation>This error severity level is WARNING. A batch file submission may receive one or more WARNING errors and still be accepted by FinCEN (i.e., status will be "ACCEPTED-WITH-WARNINGS" as a result). Refer to the error CONTEXT to determine the location of the error, and also refer to the error code list in the corresponding form type's batch technical guide to determine what action to take in response to the specific error code.</xs:documentation>				</xs:annotation>			</xs:enumeration>			<xs:enumeration value="FATAL">				<xs:annotation>					<xs:documentation>This error severity level is FATAL. A batch file that receives a FATAL error will be rejected by FinCEN (i.e., status will be "REJECTED" as a result). Refer to the error code list in the corresponding form type's batch technical guide to determine what action to take in response to the specific error code.</xs:documentation>				</xs:annotation>			</xs:enumeration>		</xs:restriction>	</xs:simpleType>	<xs:simpleType name="sdtmBatchFormType">		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">			<xs:enumeration value="CTRXST">				<xs:annotation>					<xs:documentation>Currency Transaction Report, filed via batch SFTP. The corresponding tracking ID will start with CXST (e.g., CXST26-00123456).</xs:documentation>				</xs:annotation>			</xs:enumeration>			<xs:enumeration value="SARXST">				<xs:annotation>					<xs:documentation>Suspicious Activity Report, filed via batch SFTP. The corresponding tracking ID will start with SXST (e.g., SXST26-00123456).</xs:documentation>				</xs:annotation>			</xs:enumeration>			<xs:enumeration value="DOEPXST">				<xs:annotation>					<xs:documentation>Designation of Exempt Person, filed via batch SFTP. The corresponding tracking ID will start with DPXST (e.g., DPXST26-00123456).</xs:documentation>				</xs:annotation>			</xs:enumeration>			<xs:enumeration value="FBARXST">				<xs:annotation>					<xs:documentation>Report of Foreign Bank and Financial Accounts, filed via batch SFTP. The corresponding tracking ID will start with FXST (e.g., FXST26-00123456).</xs:documentation>				</xs:annotation>			</xs:enumeration>			<xs:enumeration value="8300XST">				<xs:annotation>					<xs:documentation>Report of Cash Payments Over $10,000 Received in a Trade or Business, filed via batch SFTP. The corresponding tracking ID will start with CPXST (e.g., CPXST26-00123456).</xs:documentation>				</xs:annotation>			</xs:enumeration>			<xs:enumeration value="RERXST">				<xs:annotation>					<xs:documentation>Real Estate Report, filed via batch SFTP. The corresponding tracking ID will start with REST (e.g., REST26-00123456).</xs:documentation>				</xs:annotation>			</xs:enumeration>		</xs:restriction>	</xs:simpleType></xs:schema>